.TH "MIDIINPUT.MIDIMESSAGE_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MIDIInput.midimessage_event \- MIDIInput: midimessage event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[CR]midimessage\f[R] event of the Web MIDI API is fired when the
MIDI port corresponding to this \f[CR]MIDIInput\f[R] finishes receiving
one or more MIDI messages.
An instance of \f[CR]MIDIMessageEvent\f[R] containing the message that
was received is passed to the event handler.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqmidimessage\(dq, (event) => { })

onmidimessage = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MIDIMessageEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
In the following example \f[CR]midimessage\f[R] events are listened for
on all input ports.
When a message is received the \f[CR]MIDIMessageEvent.data\f[R] property
is printed to the console.
.IP
.EX
inputs.forEach((input) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  input.onmidimessage = (message) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    console.log(message.data);
  };
});
.EE
